gGP(){return"Check-raise as a trap; they c-bet too frequently."},
gHg(){return"Widen your 3-bet calling range vs. their opens."},
gGS(){return"Don't bloat pots out of position with marginal hands \u2014 keep the pot small or play back in position."},
gH7(){return"Respect their bets \u2014 they have range discipline."},
gGx(){return"3-bet as a steal from late position; they fold the bottom of their range."},
gGT(){return"Don't pay off their river bets \u2014 bluff-catch tighter; when they fire, they have it."},
gGC(){return"Apply positional pressure \u2014 float and barrel when they c-bet and then give up."},
gHc(){return"Trap with strong hands \u2014 let them build the pot."},
gGU(){return"Don't semi-bluff; let them hang themselves with their aggression."},
gGL(){return"Call down with any pair or decent draw \u2014 they over-represent constantly."},
gGR(){return"Don't bet-fold marginal hands \u2014 they exploit overfolding."},
gH4(){return"Mix up your own lines; they will find and exploit any pattern."},
gGz(){return"3-bet and squeeze vs. their opens \u2014 their range is weak."},
gH_(){return"Fold to their raises unless you have a premium hand."},
gH1(){return"Isolate their limps with a 3\u20134\xd7 raise."},
gGB(){return"4-bet light for value; widen your flatting range vs. their 3-bets."},
gGV(){return"Flat your strong 3-bets in position and let them barrel; 5-bet only premiums. Call their 4-bet a touch wider with hands that flop well."},
gGA(){return"3-bet them liberally as a steal from BTN and CO."},
gGy(){return"3-bet for value only (and size up) \u2014 don't 3-bet bluff. Then barrel postflop; they peel too wide."},
gH9(){return"Squeeze when they cold-call behind \u2014 they will often fold."},
gHb(){return"Tighten your cold-calls in front of them, and flat your premiums to trap the squeeze."},
gHa(){return"Steal relentlessly from the CO/BTN/SB \u2014 they surrender their blinds too cheaply."},
gGQ(){return"Check-raise their c-bets more freely \u2014 they bet too mechanically."},
gGX(){return"Float in position and take the pot away on the turn."},
gGH(){return"Bet when they check \u2014 they give up with little fight."},
gGK(){return"C-bet relentlessly with a small size \u2014 they fold far too often to the first barrel."},
gGI(){return"Bluff-catch lighter, and don't fold the flop planning to fold the turn \u2014 they keep firing without the goods."},
gGW(){return"Float the flop in position and take it away on the turn when they check \u2014 they're one-and-done."},
gGE(){return"Barrel turn and river for value and as a bluff, and size up \u2014 make their wide floats pay."},
gH3(){return"Their leads are usually a weak made hand or a draw \u2014 raise your value to deny equity; respect only a big lead into multiway."},
gGN(){return"Call rivers lighter \u2014 they over-bluff missed draws."},
gGZ(){return"Fold to large bets unless you have the nuts or near-nuts."},
gGJ(){return"Bluff them on boards where their value range is capped."},
gHd(){return"Triple-barrel bluff rivers more, especially on scare cards \u2014 they hero-fold too often."},
gGF(){return"Be cautious when they check-call passively \u2014 they may be trapping."},
gGG(){return"Bet smaller on boards where they check-raise \u2014 or check behind for pot control."},
gHe(){return"Use their bet sizing as a tell: fold marginal hands to the big bets, attack the small ones."},
gH6(){return"Pile on the pressure near the bubble \u2014 open and re-shove on their stack; they fold to survive."},
gGO(){return"Call their short-stack shoves wider \u2014 they jam far too light to fold equity."},
